      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p28-q15-answer",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For example, ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "7,\\;7,\\;10,\\;11",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", or ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "6,\\;7,\\;11,\\;11",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", from left to right. All completions are ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "t,\\;7,\\;17-t,\\;11",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", where ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "6\\le t\\le7",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p28-q15-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Last card 11, middle card 7; the remaining pair totals 17.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The last card is $5+6=11$, and the middle card is $7$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Total of five cards}&=5\\times8\\\\\\text{Total of five cards}&=40\\\\\\text{Second card}+\\text{fourth card}&=40-5-7-11\\\\\\text{Second card}+\\text{fourth card}&=17\\end{align*}$$\n\nChoosing $7$ and $10$ gives the missing numbers $7,\\;7,\\;10,\\;11$. Choosing $6$ and $11$ gives $6,\\;7,\\;11,\\;11$.\n\nMore generally, let the second card be $t$. The complete ordered list is $5,\\;t,\\;7,\\;17-t,\\;11$, with $6\\le t\\le7$. These bounds keep the second card at most $7$ and the fourth card at most $11$; no integer restriction is given.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
